.superpowers/
.worktrees/
.cursor/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.env
*.db
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
apps/story-timeline/exports/
apps/utety-chat/data/exports/
=*

# Store console TUI (repo-root runtime artifacts)
/data/
/.venv-dev/

# willow-mcp project sync output — the rendered Claude Code settings (real
# python path, live WILLOW_DEV_SAFE_ROOT, agent identity). Machine-local sync
# artifact, not repo content; the committed .claude/settings.json symlink it
# replaced (a dead willow-2.0 pointer) was removed 2026-08-17.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Willow runtime — agent identity + ephemeral git worktrees
.willow/active-agent
worktrees/
tools/.seam-receipts/
/SAFE/
*.seam.json
*.receipt.json
.sandbox/

# sap_gate.py's dev-only key custody + signing-event ledger (D4) — never
# committed even in dev; real custody is the D7 vault, not this repo.
stores/.sap_gate_keys/
stores/.sap_gate_ledger.jsonl

# principal.py's dev-only identity store (D11) — minted builder_ids and the
# GitHub accounts bound to them. Same reason: dev-only stand-in for a real
# backing store, and identity rows are not repo content.
stores/.principals/

# session.py's dev-only session store (D11) — session token hashes and their
# expiry/revocation state. Same reason: dev-only stand-in for a real backing
# store, and session rows are not repo content.
stores/.sessions/

# checkpoint_memory.py's dev-only Nestor checkpoint stores (D9/D12) — one
# SqliteStore file per builder_id, plus the shared pedagogy ledger. Same
# reason as .principals/.sessions above: dev-only stand-in, and a builder's
# checkpoint-memory rows are not repo content. (*.db and /data/ above already
# cover pieces of this; listed explicitly for the same reason .principals/
# and .sessions/ are, rather than relying on the broader globs.)
stores/.checkpoints/

# quota.py's dev-only per-builder fairness state (D6) — active lease rows
# and recorded sandbox-seconds. Same reason as the three stores above:
# dev-only stand-in for a real backing store, not repo content. (Found
# missing in review, 2026-08-02 — every sibling store in this family has
# this entry; this one didn't.)
stores/.quotas/

# .mcp.json's "nestor" entry's local vault (fleet give-back, 2026-08-13) —
# the operator's own copy of the decision-graph oracle `nestor serve` reads
# from and `tools/decisions_boot.py`'s best-effort cross-check queries over
# the real MCP protocol. Same reason as every sibling store above: dev-only
# stand-in for the operator's real vault (stores/decisions/README.md), not
# repo content. *.db above already covers the SQLite file; the directory and
# ledger.jsonl are listed explicitly for the same reason .principals/
# .sessions/.checkpoints/.quotas are.
stores/decisions/.nestor/
